<p></p>
<i>The results of this survey indicate that banks
  consistently tightened lending standards and loan terms, on net,
  between 1998 and 2003, but generally eased standards and terms
  throughout 2004 and into early 2005. Other sources suggest that
  average spreads on syndicated C&amp;I loans are now near levels last
  reached before lending terms began to tighten in 
  1998.  Questions 7-9 ask how your bank's
  current C&amp;I lending standards and terms compare with the standards and
  terms your institution offered on similar loans in the 1996-1997 period.</i>
